[E0323] Error: `[i64; 3]` does not give up its elements
    ╭─[ err/208_what_gives_up_nothing/main.wip:15:14 ]
    │
 15 │     for n in move numbers {}
    │              ──────┬─────  
    │                    ╰─────── `move` takes each element
    │ 
    │ Help: walk it without `move`, and each element is lent to the loop: `for x in c`
    │ 
    │ Note: `for x in move c` walks `c.intoIterator()`, which a `Vec`, a `Deque`, a `Set` and a `Map` answer, and a type of your own by `extend …: IntoIterator<I>`
────╯
